      api_key: "os.environ/GEMINI_API_KEY_TIGERBLUE77"

  # Served, but not routed to: it is an agent, not a chat model, and it is paid. Checked 2026-09-27:
  # "ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models/deep-research-pro-preview-12-2025" gives its "Agent code"
  # under the "Interactions API", and ".../docs/deep-research" says the agent "is exclusively
  # available using the Interactions API. You cannot access it through generate_content" -- so not
  # through the chat-completions call LiteLLM's "gemini/" provider makes either. ".../docs/pricing"
  # charges its inference "at standard Gemini list rates", and its model page says it is "Powered
  # by Gemini 3.1 Pro", whose free tier is "Not available" (above).
  # - model_name: deep-research-pro
  #   litellm_params:
  #     model: gemini/deep-research-pro-preview-12-2025
  #     api_base: "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/"
  #     api_key: "os.environ/GEMINI_API_KEY_TIGERBLUE77"

  # Gemma 4 through the Gemini API itself, added 2026-09-27. Free: the "Gemma 4" table of
  # "ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing" gives "Free of charge" for input and output on the free
  # tier, and "Not available" on the paid one. Released there 2026-04-02 (".../docs/changelog"), with
  # function calling shown on "ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/core/gemma_on_gemini_api". The same weights
  # as OpenRouter's "gemma-4-31b-free" and "gemma-4-26b-free" further down, and ranked just ahead of
